WEBVTT

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:22.088
Though you are so close,
Kore hodo soba ni

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:26.593
I cannot tell you how I feel.
Iru no ni tsutaerarezu

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:30.663
The more strongly I feel,
Tsuyoku omou hodo

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:35.268
the harder it is for me to find the words.
Kotoba ga mitsukaranai

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:43.309
What is sad is not fate...
Kanashii no wa unmei ja nakute

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:54.083
...but that all encounters come to an end.
Deai no subete ni owari ga aru koto

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:58.525
O incomplete beings,
Mikan naru mono

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:02.962
awaken, for beyond the night...
mezameyo yoru o koetara

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:07.033
At the end of the desert...
Sabaku no hate ni

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:14.701
...the truth surely awaits you.
Shinjitsu ga matteru yo kitto

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.228
Kamui...

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.164
Kamui...

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:48.835
The gray wolf was dozing.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:52.778
Did he live with humans in some bygone day?

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.716
He recalls the girl's soft hand with fondness.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:24.004
Right then, he was in a place
far removed from that past.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.979
What he could see ahead
that he ran in pursuit of...

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.940
...was a legend.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:39.490
Fairy Visions

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:42.562
Hmm, let me think.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:43.663
Shall we head that way?

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.290
Which way is "that way"?

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:49.135
Come on, you remember!
To the weird shaped rock.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.830
The one that looked like Old Man Nor's face.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.805
That'll mean doubling back.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.239
I'd like to drive in a more logical manner here.

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:59.145
Well, sure, I'm depending on you
to drive in a logical manner.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.080
So that we don't waste any fuel...

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.241
...and keep from wearing out the
drive wheel as much as possible.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.519
Don't you think this is an
awfully arbitrary request?

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.248
If you're going to insist, care to do it yourself?

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:13.152
I won't mind, but I'd end up
driving even more illogically.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.084
Nevermind. I'll do it.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.065
Honoka, Millie's calling for you.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:19.622
What?

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.126
What's up, Millie?

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.433
Hey, why do you have so many?

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:28.802
Why? Well...

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.372
It represents a lack of financial sense.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:33.343
Shuddup!

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:36.514
You know, guns are standard
equipment in the desert.

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.778
Two should be more than enough.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:42.285
What's wrong with having a hobby or two?!

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:43.611
Hono.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:47.290
Could I maybe have one of these?

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:48.521
What?

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:49.792
No?

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.864
I don't mind, but...

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.024
Have you ever fired one?

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:57.770
No, but my father had said
he'd teach me someday.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.238
Because it's necessary in the desert.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.266
Sure, you can have whichever one you want.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.104
Thank you!

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.343
This might be a little heavy.

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.648
Maybe this one's better.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.915
But... which one should I take?

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:44.009
It was a carefree journey.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:47.120
If they found a rocky formation
with a funny shape,

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.382
they would stop to enjoy it.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.625
"Nebulous memories of the past,"

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.456
"The future, yet to be determined,"

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.922
"The light of distant galaxies,"
"The light of distant galaxies,"

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:58.861
"The mirage before your eyes,"
"The mirage before your eyes,"

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:02.065
"For there is nothing that is certain,"
"For there is nothing that is certain,"

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.959
"You can pursue your dreams."
"You can pursue your dreams."

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:09.975
Under a sky full of stars, they would
recite Donna Myftee's poems.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.915
And if the sunset was beautiful,

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.110
they would stay and watch forever.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:26.522
Millie seems to be enjoying
this journey as well.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:29.062
Yes, but...

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:30.188
What is it?

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:34.322
I feel like they have yet to
repair the rift between them...

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:35.659
You can tell this?

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:40.864
I can merely see it as a
psychological phenomenon.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:46.236
I'm afraid I can't fully grasp
the significance beyond that.

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:48.705
People are far too complicated.

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:50.112
True.

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.409
Perhaps it's just that,

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:54.449
which makes them so beautiful, though.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:05.391
Before, I used to not like sunsets
in the desert very much.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:06.596
Why not?

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:09.893
They meant my father would start working.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.671
When night fell,

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:14.374
all sorts of people would come
and he had to work, right?

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:17.400
And then I'd be left alone, so...

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:20.408
Hey, you know, Millie...

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:25.040
I mean, don't you wish your teacher
Paife could've seen that sunset, too?

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:29.213
Yeah! I think she wanted to come with us.

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:30.755
She was puffing out her cheeks in a sulk!

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.292
I'm amazed you could tell.

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:36.129
She's sort of... you know, expressionless.

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:38.631
At first, I was a little scared of her.

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:39.859
Oh, I knew it.

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:44.832
What's this? A cold?

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:48.741
But she's changed quite a bit.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:52.345
Oh, yeah, there was a time when she
took a long break a while back,

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:53.869
and she's been especially different since then.

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:16.931
I wonder what they're doing right about now.

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:25.511
In order to be able to immediately
draw her sword if anything happened,

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:28.344
Honoka does not walk hand-in-hand with Millie.

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.474
Millie also understood this.

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:36.083
Even without holding hands,
they were together at heart.

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:38.880
They both believed this.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.289
Until now...

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:45.460
Insignificant words would bring
great turmoil to Millie's heart.

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:47.793
On this carefree... No.

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:51.826
In truth, they only pretended to
be carefree on this journey...

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:57.134
...and Honoka dealt with Millie
as if she treaded on thin ice.

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:02.281
She would ask Millie to her face,
once and for all...

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:05.978
Honoka's heart was beginning to shift.

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:09.351
Hono.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.683
Going too far would be...

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.020
You're right.

00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:19.231
Millie.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.321
What is it?

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.128
Let me ask you honestly.

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:26.372
Is there anything that you're
hurting over or agonizing about?

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:26.997
What?

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.175
I heard from Paife.

00:08:29.175 --> 00:08:33.271
That you fell asleep in class
and wouldn't wake up.

00:08:33.446 --> 00:08:34.814
Oh...

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:35.848
That.

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:39.340
Somehow, it was really
comfortable and I fell asleep.

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:44.520
I asked her not to tell anyone,
because it's so embarrassing.

00:08:44.824 --> 00:08:47.493
Millie, you shouldn't hide things.

00:08:47.493 --> 00:08:50.429
That's not something that happens normally.

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:53.165
But you know, there's nothing wrong with me.

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:55.156
Teacher said so, too.

00:08:55.468 --> 00:08:57.095
That's why I'm asking.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:01.597
Millie, are you sleeping all right at
night? What about your appetite?

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:06.268
Come on, we're all worried about you.

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:10.616
It's not like I can always be with you,

00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:13.449
so I'm not in any position to talk big, but...

00:09:13.886 --> 00:09:15.087
Is that why?

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:15.519
What?

00:09:15.922 --> 00:09:17.913
Is that why you invited me along?

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.115
Taking time off from work...

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:21.819
Then...

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:24.153
Then I wish I hadn't come!

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:26.022
Millie?

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:30.529
If I was going to be in your way,
I wish I hadn't come along!

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:33.266
Millie, why?

00:09:33.606 --> 00:09:36.507
Don't just... Don't just worry
about me without even asking!

00:09:36.976 --> 00:09:40.912
I can... I can keep going on my own, too!

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:43.147
I want to work hard on my own...

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:45.848
...and become like you!

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.520
Millie, l-I...

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:51.952
You don't have to worry!

00:09:52.725 --> 00:09:55.023
If I'm in your way,

00:09:55.895 --> 00:09:57.797
you don't have to be with me!

00:09:57.797 --> 00:09:59.822
I hate you, Hono!

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:01.622
Millie?!

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:05.302
Millie!

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:07.535
Honoka!

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.508
Bogie, I don't have time to talk right now.

00:10:10.643 --> 00:10:11.632
Turn back right now!

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:14.936
The sand temperature is rapidly
rising up ahead of you!

00:10:18.184 --> 00:10:18.980
Millie!

00:10:28.861 --> 00:10:30.796
Crap! An ant lion trap!

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:32.423
No! That's a...

00:10:36.702 --> 00:10:37.600
Millie!

00:10:56.789 --> 00:10:58.347
It's... a Pancake!

00:11:14.106 --> 00:11:15.130
Damn it!

00:11:30.623 --> 00:11:31.783
Millie!

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:37.289
Honoka!

00:11:40.466 --> 00:11:41.728
Honoka, move aside!

00:11:42.101 --> 00:11:44.797
It's no use! Its body is inside the sand, and...

00:11:46.238 --> 00:11:47.705
...Millie's in there, too!

00:11:56.615 --> 00:11:57.639
Don't surrender.

00:12:00.352 --> 00:12:02.946
At any rate, I have to get inside that hollow!

00:12:03.656 --> 00:12:05.954
You can't! Once you fall in,
you'll never get out of there!

00:12:06.659 --> 00:12:07.455
Millie!

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.022
Millie!

00:12:14.867 --> 00:12:16.095
Don't surrender.

00:12:17.069 --> 00:12:18.502
Don't give up.

00:12:19.105 --> 00:12:20.504
Don't give up, Millie!

00:12:21.474 --> 00:12:22.998
Hono?

00:12:23.142 --> 00:12:24.973
Millie!

00:12:29.482 --> 00:12:30.107
What was that?

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:02.610
It's coming out! The Pancake's true body!

00:13:19.131 --> 00:13:20.029
Got it.

00:13:21.167 --> 00:13:22.429
Millie.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:51.694
Honoka!

00:13:53.499 --> 00:13:54.158
Miss Honoka!

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:55.565
Iks!

00:13:56.735 --> 00:13:57.570
Take Millie!

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:58.832
Y-Yes!

00:14:00.673 --> 00:14:01.332
Miss Honoka!

00:14:52.324 --> 00:14:53.552
She's fine.

00:14:53.893 --> 00:14:55.628
She has no injuries.

00:14:55.628 --> 00:14:57.357
She should regain consciousness in time.

00:14:59.198 --> 00:15:01.826
Millie, I'm sorry.

00:15:04.937 --> 00:15:06.404
It was my mistake.

00:15:06.472 --> 00:15:09.032
If I had detected its presence a little earlier...

00:15:09.742 --> 00:15:12.575
You're wrong, Bogie. It's me.

00:15:12.745 --> 00:15:13.973
It's my fault.

00:15:14.146 --> 00:15:17.445
I can't believe it! What am I doing?!

00:15:18.083 --> 00:15:21.052
I was... I was about to lose Millie.

00:15:22.388 --> 00:15:23.412
Miss Honoka...

00:15:23.856 --> 00:15:25.551
I'm so stupid.

00:15:25.724 --> 00:15:27.123
Really stupid.

00:15:27.626 --> 00:15:31.062
I didn't understand how Millie felt at all.

00:15:31.864 --> 00:15:36.927
I didn't even realize my worrying about
her was itself a burden for her.

00:15:38.404 --> 00:15:40.599
She'd been straining herself all this time.

00:15:41.273 --> 00:15:44.674
Thinking about how she could
survive on her own...

00:15:45.177 --> 00:15:48.180
About how she could gain independence...

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:50.045
...without causing anyone trouble.

00:15:54.887 --> 00:15:55.444
Millie.

00:15:56.789 --> 00:15:58.290
Fai... ry...

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.552
Huh? What?

00:15:59.892 --> 00:16:01.427
The Fairy...

00:16:01.427 --> 00:16:03.486
Don't push yourself yet, Millie.

00:16:12.404 --> 00:16:13.371
That's...

00:16:13.572 --> 00:16:16.803
It can't be... The Desert Fairy?

00:16:17.643 --> 00:16:18.803
The Star Seed...

00:16:19.878 --> 00:16:22.039
She called out to me.

00:16:22.548 --> 00:16:27.076
The whole time I was falling into the sand...

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:31.654
She told me, "Don't surrender. Don't give up."

00:16:32.191 --> 00:16:34.159
Along with you.

00:16:34.727 --> 00:16:35.489
With me?

00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.478
It disappeared...

00:17:01.653 --> 00:17:02.517
Where did it...

00:17:15.801 --> 00:17:16.768
Miss Millie?

00:17:20.739 --> 00:17:23.264
Millie, that wolf...

00:17:23.675 --> 00:17:25.939
Yeah, I know.

00:17:28.147 --> 00:17:29.045
Thank you.

00:17:36.722 --> 00:17:39.748
That wolf spoke to me.

00:17:40.626 --> 00:17:42.856
"What is that being?"

00:17:43.362 --> 00:17:44.989
Honoka wondered.

00:17:45.998 --> 00:17:49.068
The being that had stood before
Honoka's eyes until just then...

00:17:49.068 --> 00:17:50.968
...was no ordinary wolf.

00:17:52.071 --> 00:17:54.972
The creature with surpassing intelligence...

00:17:55.407 --> 00:17:57.705
...vanished into the moonlit night.

00:17:58.877 --> 00:18:00.003
Hono.

00:18:00.145 --> 00:18:00.702
What?

00:18:01.213 --> 00:18:02.510
I'm sorry.

00:18:02.781 --> 00:18:05.648
I lied when I said I hated you.

00:18:06.218 --> 00:18:07.344
Millie...

00:18:07.986 --> 00:18:09.578
I know, Millie.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:16.618
I... I love you, Hono, but I'm in your way!

00:18:16.895 --> 00:18:19.329
Millie, that's not...

00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:24.525
I can't do anything...

00:18:26.238 --> 00:18:29.696
I'll just be in your way...

00:18:31.343 --> 00:18:32.435
Millie...

00:18:34.146 --> 00:18:35.477
Millie.

00:18:46.425 --> 00:18:47.687
Has she fallen asleep?

00:18:48.627 --> 00:18:49.389
Yeah.

00:18:54.867 --> 00:18:57.233
Something Old Man Nor said...

00:18:57.736 --> 00:18:58.566
What?

00:18:58.904 --> 00:19:02.841
A long time ago, Old Man Nor said something,

00:19:02.841 --> 00:19:06.242
but I didn't think much of it at the time.

00:19:08.347 --> 00:19:10.542
Millie sure is a tough girl.

00:19:11.116 --> 00:19:11.741
Yeah.

00:19:12.284 --> 00:19:14.980
Though, being too tough
can also be worrisome.

00:19:16.288 --> 00:19:20.054
She's a child, so it's only natural
that she lacks strength.

00:19:20.592 --> 00:19:23.026
It's only natural that there
are some things she can't do,

00:19:23.595 --> 00:19:24.118
but...

00:19:24.596 --> 00:19:28.532
Miss Millie's tough spirit will not allow for that.

00:19:29.902 --> 00:19:33.633
I... don't know anymore.

00:19:34.406 --> 00:19:37.309
What I should do for Millie...

00:19:37.309 --> 00:19:39.243
What can I do for her?

00:19:39.711 --> 00:19:40.405
No...

00:19:41.146 --> 00:19:44.707
Maybe thinking that there's
something I can do for her...

00:19:45.517 --> 00:19:47.075
...is arrogant to begin with.

00:19:48.353 --> 00:19:50.218
It's a simple matter.

00:19:50.322 --> 00:19:52.057
Just say it to her.

00:19:52.057 --> 00:19:54.617
Say, "You're not in my way."

00:19:55.894 --> 00:19:58.624
And Millie will probably think...

00:19:59.798 --> 00:20:03.029
...that I'm just saying that out
of consideration for her.

00:20:03.335 --> 00:20:05.269
Words like that alone won't...

00:20:06.371 --> 00:20:08.999
Humans are too complicated.

00:20:10.209 --> 00:20:11.801
That being earlier...

00:20:12.511 --> 00:20:16.447
That wolf seems to have gone off
in pursuit of the Desert Fairy.

00:20:16.682 --> 00:20:18.707
Why don't we see where it goes?

00:20:20.152 --> 00:20:21.210
Go after the wolf?

00:20:36.001 --> 00:20:37.559
What are you looking at?

00:20:39.671 --> 00:20:41.036
I was searching...

00:20:41.673 --> 00:20:44.267
For the route we'd take from here on out.

00:20:45.143 --> 00:20:46.110
Did you find it?

00:20:47.145 --> 00:20:50.273
I don't think I'll be able to
drive in a logical manner.

00:20:51.149 --> 00:20:52.912
You'll receive a scolding from Mr. Bogie.

00:20:53.986 --> 00:20:55.044
You're right.

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:59.256
But I've decided on the path you chose for us.

00:20:59.958 --> 00:21:01.425
In pursuit of the wolf?

00:21:01.627 --> 00:21:05.757
I haven't thanked him properly
for saving Millie anyway.

00:21:06.231 --> 00:21:07.357
That is true.

00:21:07.666 --> 00:21:08.900
I came out here...

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:13.071
...to show Millie the wondrous
things in the desert.

00:21:13.071 --> 00:21:16.063
That wolf and the Desert Fairy...

00:21:16.508 --> 00:21:18.669
There's nothing more wondrous
than them, right?

00:21:19.177 --> 00:21:19.871
Let's go!

00:21:20.412 --> 00:21:21.276
Yes.

00:21:23.015 --> 00:21:24.883
"Let's go!"

00:21:24.883 --> 00:21:28.114
Honoka murmured it to herself
in her heart once more.

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:31.123
Chasing after the wolf and the Fairy...

00:21:31.123 --> 00:21:34.593
...could possibly lead to the path...

00:21:34.593 --> 00:21:36.959
...that she and Millie would
follow from here on out.

00:21:38.196 --> 00:21:40.255
She had no basis for thinking that.

00:21:40.332 --> 00:21:43.631
It was merely a faint hope.

00:21:53.045 --> 00:21:56.515
An intersection waiting for morning...
Asa o matteiru kousaten ga

00:21:56.515 --> 00:22:00.519
...cradling an abandoned cat that wandered in.
Mayoikonda sute-neko o daiteiru

00:22:00.519 --> 00:22:03.121
Red and green and yellow.
Aka to ao to kiiro

00:22:03.121 --> 00:22:06.022
It is simply gentle.
Sore wa tada yasashii

00:22:06.758 --> 00:22:10.228
Stopping just after dawn,
Akegata-sugi ni furiyanda

00:22:10.228 --> 00:22:14.266
a misty rain made a screen of water.
Kosame ga tsukutta mizu no sukuriin ga

00:22:14.266 --> 00:22:16.802
Until that time when it dries,
Kawaku sono toki made

00:22:16.802 --> 00:22:19.771
it is simply gentle
Sore wa tada yasashii

00:22:20.005 --> 00:22:23.508
More than small coincidences like that,
Sonna chiisana guuzen yori mo

00:22:23.508 --> 00:22:26.912
the fact that you are there...
Kimi ga soko ni iru koto ga

00:22:26.912 --> 00:22:30.382
...cannot be a small thing, I think.
Chiisai hazu ga nai to omounda

00:22:30.382 --> 00:22:33.977
Even though it's obvious.
Atarimae nandakedo

00:22:35.687 --> 00:22:42.461
It must be sad not to have anyone.
Daremo inai to kanashii koto deshou

00:22:42.461 --> 00:22:49.401
Now, come on out to where the sun is shining.
Saa hi no ataru basho e dete-oide

00:22:49.401 --> 00:22:56.241
Even the several incidents that trouble you...
Kimi o komaraseru ikutsuka no dekigoto mo

00:22:56.241 --> 00:23:01.178
...are coincidences of yesterdays past.
Kinou izen no guuzen nanda yo

00:23:03.048 --> 00:23:08.953
Though, I'm sure you actually know that already.
Hontou wa wakatteru to omou kedo

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.855
Preview

00:23:17.529 --> 00:23:18.359
Leon.

00:23:18.797 --> 00:23:21.129
The hunter that was after the Desert Fairy...

00:23:21.466 --> 00:23:25.527
After he fired shots at that wolf,
he wished to fight with me.

00:23:26.071 --> 00:23:27.402
Menacing blades...

00:23:27.706 --> 00:23:29.173
Swords crossed...

00:23:29.441 --> 00:23:32.342
And a chest pierced...

00:23:32.944 --> 00:23:35.572
The light of my life grows faint...

00:23:36.481 --> 00:23:40.051
Next time on
The Third - The Girl With The Blue Eye,

00:23:40.051 --> 00:23:42.020
episode 15, "Night of the Sandstorm".

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.288
Night of the Sandstorm
episode 15, "Night of the Sandstorm".

00:23:43.288 --> 00:23:44.880
Night of the Sandstorm
